  "text": "Every time you call a recursive function in Python, CPython allocates an entire stack frame in memory. This stack frame stores the function's local variables, bytecode instruction pointer, and evaluation stack. Go too deep, and Python halts your program with a fatal RecursionError. By default, the call stack limit is strictly capped at just one thousand frames to prevent an operating system crash. Instead of blowing up the call stack, convert your recursive logic to an iterative loop using collections deque. A deque runs entirely in heap memory, executes significantly faster, and completely eliminates stack frame allocation overhead.",
